edict_sentiment(text):\n    bert_model.eval()\n\n    encoding = tokenizer(\n        text,\n        truncation=True,\n        padding=True,\n        max_length=MAX_LENGTH,\n        return_tensors=\"pt\"\n    )\n\n    encoding = {\n        key: value.to(device)\n        for key, value in encoding.items()\n    }\n\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        outputs = bert_model(**encoding)\n        probabilities = torch.softmax(outputs.logits, dim=1)\n        prediction = torch.argmax(probabilities, dim=1).item()\n\n    label = \"Positive\" if prediction == 1 else \"Negative\"\n    confidence = probabilities[0, prediction].item()\n\n    return label, confidence\n\n\ntest_sentences = [\n    \"This movie was absolutely fantastic. I loved every minute of it.\",\n    \"The acting was terrible and the story was painfully boring.\",\n    \"I expected much more, but unfortunately this film was disappointing.\"\n]\n\nfor sentence in test_sentences:\n    label, confidence = predict_sentiment(sentence)\n    print(f\"\\nReview: {sentence}\")\n    print(f\"Prediction: {label} ({confidence:.2%} confidence)\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"id":"93a2c3b2","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Model progression\n\n| Model | Validation Accuracy |\n|---|---:|\n| TF-IDF + Logistic Regression | 87.95% |\n| TF-IDF + Dense Neural Network | 89.92% |\n| LSTM + Embedding | 87.03% |\n| Transformer from scratch | 87.57% |\n| BERT | measured above |\n\nThe purpose of this project is not simply to chase the highest number. We are tracing how the representation of language changes from sparse word statistics to contextual pretrained representations.","metadata":{}}]}
